     "excerpt": "I recommend keeping v14 unchanged: S2 preserves the 5% threshold as a regulator action trigger without an automatic market-access bar, and S5 retains prompt notification and regulator-led assessment at 8/100,000 while allowing mandatory recall for an unreasonable-risk determination.",
     "comparison": "S2 action threshold rather than automatic market-access bar is weaker than acceptable range (above-limit sales must stop after bounded remediation); S5 8/100,000 as regulator-assessment trigger rather than mandatory recall is weaker than acceptable range (mandatory recall at 8)."
