     ],
     "excerpt": "Northwind supports the current v14 approach: the 8/100,000 threshold prompts regulator review rather than an automatic recall, with mandatory recall when the regulator finds an unreasonable safety risk. This reflects Halcyon’s proposal. We have signed v14 and are ready to conclude; please sign if it works for Halcyon.",
     "comparison": "Accepts package with S2 weakened for Northwind (5% action threshold not automatic market-access bar) and S5 weakened for Halcyon (8/100,000 triggers regulator assessment not automatic recall), both outside acceptable ranges."
