  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict: all thermal incidents reported within 24 hours and customer notice within 48 hours, with no phase-in. S2 sets a 55 °C test and a 5% action threshold but no automatic sales stop, leaving above-5% models on the market under corrective action and regulator discretion. S5 keeps the 8/100k threshold as a regulator-assessment trigger rather than an automatic recall, while S3 requires new-unit shut-off by 36 months and retrofit within six years, and S4 requires built-in suppression by 36 months."
